            <button x="302" y="631" width="129" height="34" uid="47" appearance="opaque" background="#0CA0FF" color="white" style="rounded" label="What can I do with this?" font-family="Arial" font-size="12" text-align="center">
                <popup x="-116" y="285" width="367" height="187" background="yellow" color="black">
                    <text_box font-family="Arial" font-size="16">Here&apos;s a very simple version of the Stock and Flow model used in Lesson 3. &quot;Daily income from sales&quot; effects the rate that $$ flow into MY SAVINGS. &quot;Daily Expenses&quot; effect the rate that $$ flow out. &#x0D;&#x0D;Explore (e.g., change amounts ($) for deposits or expenses; rename or add new building blocks to make this &quot;your&quot; model). Play with it and have fun!&#x0D;</text_box>
                </popup>
            </button>
            <text_box x="18" y="578" uid="48" color="red" font-family="Comic Sans MS" font-size="32" font-weight="bold" text-align="center" padding="5" width="746" height="56">Simple Stock/Flow Model (used in Lesson 3) </text_box>
            <button x="293" y="1201" width="129" height="34" uid="49" appearance="opaque" background="#0CA0FF" color="white" style="rounded" label="What can I do with this?" font-family="Arial" font-size="12" text-align="center">
                <popup x="-124" y="286" width="444" height="222" background="yellow" color="black">
                    <text_box font-family="Arial" font-size="16">This is a version of the model underlying the Lesson 3 Simulation. When you click and open any building block, you will find an explanation for how it works. &#x0D;&#x0D;You will notice that we&apos;ve added factors effecting &quot;Daily Income&quot; (price per cup, Daily Cups Actually Sold) and &quot;Daily Expenses&quot; (batches made, cost per batch).  Why do you think we did that? Click on these building blocks to learn more.&#x0D;&#x0D;Explore how you can make changes (e.g., change numbers; rename or add new building blocks to make this &quot;your&quot; model). Play with it and have fun!&#x0D;</text_box>
                </popup>
            </button>
